es added for probe_rebar.py + check_config_reads.py (scripts/ legitimate-print convention; make lint scopes src+tests so the 6754 script had missed the list silently).","timestamp":1785728208785295001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patchset 1 Verified-1: golden-path job failed exit 127 (scripts/probe-rebar.sh not found). ROOT CAUSE: gerrit-verify.yaml executes from MAIN's workflow definition against the patchset tree — a change that deletes the shell probe can never pass main's still-shell golden-path step. Consumer sweep missed this executes-from-main dimension (4th consumer class beyond the 3 enumerated in-tree ones). FIX (patchset 2/3): restore scripts/probe-rebar.sh as a 7-line transitional exec shim delegating to probe_rebar.py; created d772-6007-5d04-4101 (discovered_from) to delete the shim once this change lands and main's golden-path step is the re-pointed Python one. Shim smoke-tested locally: 140/140. Patchset 3 fixes the shim comment to cite the real follow-up ticket id.","timestamp":1785730625293170001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion evidence for the two verifier findings: (1) Assertion-parity table — the ticket scope located it in the change description by design; it exists in merged commit 04085bf03 ('Port probe-rebar.sh to Python, assertion parity', git log origin/main --grep 'rebar-ticket: f1eb'), one row per probe section mapping shell assertions to Python: all 140 runtime assertions ported 1:1 by label, 0 retired, +1 gated self-test assertion (PROBE_INJECT_FAIL) = 141 static. Verify: git show 04085bf03 --no-patch. Runtime proof both probes report '140 passed, 0 failed' pre/post port (recorded earlier on this ticket). (2) Shell file presence — scripts/probe-rebar.sh is no longer the probe: it is a 7-line exec shim delegating to scripts/probe_rebar.py, required because gerrit-verify.yaml executes from MAIN's definition (patchset 1 failed golden-path exit 127 without it). All in-tree consumers (test.yml:128, gerrit-verify.yaml:209 golden-path, anti-rot substring in test_probe_wired_into_ci.py, docs/releasing.md) invoke the Python entry point directly; shim deletion is ticket d772-6007-5d04-4101 (discovered_from this ticket), actionable only after this change is in main's workflow definition. Scope line updated to reflect the discovered executes-from-main constraint.","timestamp":1785768528981455001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AC2 evidence artifact — assertion-parity inventory, recorded verbatim from merged commit 04085bf03 (git show 04085bf03 --no-patch):\n\nAssertion-parity inventory: all 140 shell assertions ported 1:1 by label, 0 retired. Per-section counts (identical shell vs Python): create 7 (+1 gated self-test), show 6, edit 6, tags 6, links 15, claim 4, transition 9, close-guards 6, quality-gates 7, file-impact 5, scratch 4, reads 18, output-flag 8, report-json 6, lifecycle-json 11, single-reducer 4, help 10, archive 6, delete 2.\n\nSide-by-side on the same build: shell 140 passed / 0 failed; Python 140 passed / 0 failed. Self-test: PROBE_INJECT_FAIL=1 injects one failing assertion — the harness continues through all sections, reports it, exits 1 (141 executed: 140 passed, 1 failed).\n\nThis comment is the durable, repo-readable record of the AC2 parity table (the table's primary home is the merged commit message per the ticket Scope).","timestamp":1785769182650864001}],"created_at":1785640127838320001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1a803e6c-bb23-460b-832a-143f3f1a3cc8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3342-e91b-19f9-49e6"},{"link_uuid":"0a719b81-45ba-4396-8684-97864a91f35e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"909e-2a9f-daf5-4dc7"},{"link_uuid":"3c7b9f06-181f-4bbb-9efd-744eddb399c9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"08ce-0e74-07f6-414e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nprobe-rebar.sh accumulated stale assertions (08ce: 3 stale asserts against removed flags/keysets). Its missing 'set -e' is DELIBERATE harness design (continue past failures, report all) — a naive port or hardening pass would break it.\n\n## Approach\nPort to a Python probe harness (scripts/probe_rebar.py) preserving the continue-on-failure design (collect results, report all, exit non-zero if any failed — the same contract, now explicit). Assertion-parity review required: every current assertion enumerated and carried over or retired with a reason (the 08ce class came from silent drift). Do NOT add set -e semantics.\n\nShell deletion and consumer re-pointing happen in the SAME change, after the side-by-side parity run: every consumer that hard-wires the shell path is re-pointed to the Python entry point in this change, so CI and the anti-rot gate track the new harness atomically.\n\n## Scope\n- scripts/probe-rebar.sh -> scripts/probe_rebar.py (port; the shell path is retained as a 7-line transitional exec shim because gerrit-verify.yaml executes from MAIN's workflow definition, whose golden-path step still invokes the shell path until this change lands — discovered on patchset 1, Verified-1 exit 127; deletion is follow-up d772-6007-5d04-4101)\n- Consumers re-pointed in the same change (enumerated by grep for 'probe-rebar'):\n  - .github/workflows/test.yml:128 — 'bash scripts/probe-rebar.sh </dev/null' -> python invocation\n  - .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml:209 — same re-point\n  - .github/workflows/external-integration.yml:54 — comment mentioning the path; update wording\n  - tests/unit/test_probe_wired_into_ci.py — _PROBE_JOBS asserts substring 'scripts/probe-rebar.sh' in golden-path jobs; update the pinned substring to the Python entry point so the anti-rot gate keeps guarding\n  - docs/releasing.md:401,405,407 — invocation examples -> Python equivalents\n  - CHANGELOG.md + docs/experiments corpus jsonl are historical records — NOT touched.\n- Assertion inventory table in the change description (commit message).\n\n## Testing\nSelf-test: inject one failing probe -> harness continues, reports it, exits non-zero. Parity: run both harnesses against the same build before deletion, identical pass/fail verdict per assertion. tests/unit/test_probe_wired_into_ci.py green against the updated substring.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Python harness replaces the shell probe with continue-on-failure preserved.\n- [x] Assertion-parity table: every shell assertion mapped to ported/retired-with-reason.\n- [x] Side-by-side run shows identical verdicts; shell path reduced to a transitional exec shim (full deletion tracked in d772-6007-5d04-4101, required because gerrit-verify.yaml executes from main's workflow definition) with ALL enumerated consumers (workflows, anti-rot test, docs) re-pointed to the Python entry point.\n\n## 2026-08-08 resolved-report consolidation\n\nResolved report: `08ce-0e74-07f6-414e` (the three stale shell-probe assertions were incorporated into this port).\n\nFresh resolution experiment on current `origin/main`: `python scripts/probe_rebar.py` ran the full isolated end-to-end CLI probe and reported `PROBE RESULT: 140 passed, 0 failed`. This re-exercises the exact edit/tag, priority, and show/list projection assertions from the original report, so none remains stale.\n","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/probe-rebar.sh","reason":"port to Python, then delete"},{"path":"scripts/","reason":"new Python probe harness"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97"],["relates_to","08ce-0e74-07f6-414e"],["relates_to","3342-e91b-19f9-49e6"],["relates_to","909e-2a9f-daf5-4dc7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","parent_status_uuid":"fdc64001-b5d1-42a9-9379-124fd6b85989","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["shell-migration"],"ticket_id":"f1eb-5b53-f8bd-4f2b","ticket_type":"task","title":"Shell-to-Python Tier 2: probe-rebar.sh with assertion-parity review","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["43c49d77-a62c-49c5-bef0-31d2fdc16705","7c921aec-5aaa-4c91-ba9b-c2c9e6ab0ef0","fdb9c13b-0044-489a-99d8-93ce3b6f57dd","6743ae18-88b4-4163-ae90-bd5ef46fc207","df7b6ce4-d301-4b93-b4c7-fabade592eb4","81473021-2a29-4409-b235-15103ef35d03","ad15bd68-70fa-408b-8417-c6eaa33cbafb","fdc64001-b5d1-42a9-9379-124fd6b85989","18905ca5-bf44-42ec-a102-7c792bcb92fa","44bf55a0-f4a0-4978-bd42-da7f393d79c8","3c7b9f06-181f-4bbb-9efd-744eddb399c9"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659691745966001,"uuid":"2f99901b-a1b3-4173-8583-c7ac2caf0816"}